We present a measurement of the shape of the $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ differential decay rate using a sample of $pp$ collisions at $\sqrt{s}=13$ TeV, collected by the LHCb experiment and corresponding to an integrated luminosity of $9$ fb$^{-1}$. The decay rate is measured as a function of the $D_s^{*-}$ momentum in the $B_s^0$ rest frame, and the results are compared to the predictions of the Standard Model. The measurement is performed using a sample of $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ decays, where the $D_s^{*-}$ is reconstructed in the $K^-\pi^+\pi^-$ final state. The results are presented in terms of the differential decay rate as a function of the $D_s^{*-}$ momentum, and the measurements are compared to the predictions of the Standard Model. The results are also used to constrain the Wilson coefficients of the effective Hamiltonian describing the $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ decay.
